## 🔍 Core Detection Modules

### 1. YOLO Detector ([yolo_detector.py](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/src/detection/yolo_detector.py))

**Purpose:** Detects persons and cheating-related objects in video frames

**Key Features:**
- Multi-model support (nano/small/medium) for different performance needs
- Auto-detection of GPU/CPU and appropriate image sizing
- Frame skipping for performance optimization
- Tracks cheating-related objects:
  - Cell phones (class 67)
  - Books (class 73)
  - Laptops (class 63)
  - Backpacks (class 24)
  - Handbags (class 26)

**Performance:**
- Image sizes: 640px (nano/CPU), 728px (small), 1344px (medium/GPU)
- Frame skipping enabled when processing time > 100ms
- Confidence threshold: 0.4

**Key Methods:**
- [detect_frame(frame)](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/src/detection/yolo_detector.py#126-201) - Process single frame
- [draw_detections(frame, result)](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/src/detection/yolo_detector.py#326-393) - Annotate frame with bounding boxes
- [switch_model(model_size)](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/src/cheat_detection_web_app/app.py#278-285) - Change YOLO model on-the-fly
- [get_performance_stats()](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/src/detection/yolo_detector.py#408-417) - Return processing metrics

---

### 2. Pose Detector ([pose_detector.py](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/src/detection/pose_detector.py))

**Purpose:** Analyzes body pose and head orientation using MediaPipe

**Key Features:**
- Head orientation estimation (pitch, yaw, roll)
- Hand-to-face proximity detection
- Temporal smoothing for stability
- 3D pose landmark extraction (33 points)

**Head Orientation:**
- Uses 7 key landmarks (nose, eyes, mouth, shoulders)
- 3D model with solvePnP for accurate angle calculation
- Realistic limits: pitch ±45°, yaw ±90°, roll ±45°

**Hand Metrics:**
- Distance to face calculation
- Multiple proximity thresholds (very close, close, somewhat close)
- Tracks both left and right hands independently

**Optimization:**
- Model complexity: 0 (fastest)
- Detection confidence: 0.3-0.4
- Smoothing factor: 0.7
- History length: 10 frames

**Key Methods:**
- [detect(image, track_id)](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/src/detection/pose_detector.py#67-171) - Process image and return pose data
- [_estimate_head_orientation()](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/src/detection/pose_detector.py#172-229) - Calculate head angles
- [_compute_hand_metrics()](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/src/detection/pose_detector.py#230-258) - Analyze hand positions
- [_smooth_landmarks()](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/src/detection/pose_detector.py#352-369) - Apply temporal smoothing

---

### 3. Object Tracker ([object_tracker.py](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/src/detection/object_tracker.py))

**Purpose:** Maintains consistent IDs for detected persons across frames

**Key Features:**
- Centroid-based tracking algorithm
- Reappearance handling (tracks temporarily occluded persons)
- Automatic ID assignment and deregistration
- Position history tracking (30 frames)

**Parameters:**
- Max disappeared: 30 frames before deregistration
- Max distance: 50 pixels for centroid association
- Reappearance threshold: 15 frames

**Key Methods:**
- [update(detections)](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/src/detection/object_tracker.py#69-176) - Update tracks with new detections
- [register(centroid, bbox)](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/src/detection/object_tracker.py#25-32) - Add new tracked object
- [deregister(object_id)](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/src/detection/object_tracker.py#33-45) - Remove lost object
- [check_reappearance()](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/src/detection/object_tracker.py#46-68) - Match with recently disappeared objects

---

### 4. Exam Seat Manager ([exam_seat_manager.py](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/src/detection/exam_seat_manager.py))

**Purpose:** Assigns and tracks seat/zone positions for exam takers

**Key Features:**
- Dynamic zone creation based on person positions
- Zone stability scoring
- Automatic zone cleanup for empty seats
- Position history for stable assignment

**Zone Management:**
- Default zone size: 120x150 pixels
- Stability threshold: 3 frames minimum
- Empty zone timeout: 30 frames
- Cleanup timeout: 60 frames

**Key Methods:**
- [update(detections)](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/src/detection/object_tracker.py#69-176) - Update seat assignments
- [_create_zone(position, track_id)](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/src/detection/exam_seat_manager.py#227-255) - Create new zone
- [_is_in_zone(position, zone)](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/src/detection/exam_seat_manager.py#202-226) - Check zone membership
- [draw_zones(frame, assignments)](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/src/detection/exam_seat_manager.py#276-326) - Visualize zones (currently disabled)

---

### 5. Suspicion Scorer ([suspicion_scorer.py](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/src/detection/suspicion_scorer.py))

**Purpose:** Calculates suspicion scores based on behavioral analysis

**Scoring Components:**

1. **Head Orientation (0-50 points)**
   - Yaw threshold: 30° (max 30 points)
   - Pitch threshold: 20° (max 20 points)

2. **Hand-Object Proximity (0-100 points)**
   - High-risk objects (phone/book): Instant 100 points
   - Other objects: 40 points
   - Hand near face: 15 points

3. **Temporal Smoothing**
   - History length: 10 frames
   - Smoothing factor: 0.5
   - Aggressive smoothing for decreases (0.7)
   - Moderate smoothing for increases (0.3)

**Risk Classification:**
- **High Risk:** cell phone, book, notebook
- **Medium Risk:** laptop, handbag, backpack

**Key Methods:**
- [score_detection(detection)](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/src/detection/suspicion_scorer.py#39-103) - Calculate suspicion score
- [_head_component()](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/src/detection/suspicion_scorer.py#190-217) - Score head orientation
- [_hand_face_component()](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/src/detection/suspicion_scorer.py#281-327) - Score hand-face proximity
- [_hand_object_component()](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/src/detection/suspicion_scorer.py#328-388) - Score hand-object proximity
- [_smooth()](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/src/detection/suspicion_scorer.py#117-150) - Apply temporal smoothing

---

### 6. Flagged Evidence Saver ([flagged_evidence_saver.py](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/src/detection/flagged_evidence_saver.py))

**Purpose:** Automatically saves evidence when suspicion exceeds threshold

**Key Features:**
- Automatic saving when score ≥ 20/100
- Full frame + cropped regions
- JSON metadata with timestamps and reasons
- Retention policy (7 days, max 100 events)
- Privacy-focused (auto-delete old evidence)

**Saved Data Structure:**
```
output/flagged_evidence/
└── YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS_ffffff_score/
    ├── frame.jpg              # Full frame
    ├── crop_0_behavior.jpg    # Cropped person
    ├── crop_1_behavior.jpg    # Additional crops
    └── metadata.json          # Event details
```

**Metadata Contents:**
- Event ID and timestamp
- Suspicion score (0-1 and 0-100 scales)
- Behavior descriptions
- All detection data
- Crop information

**Key Methods:**
- [process_frame(frame, detections)](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/src/detection/flagged_evidence_saver.py#45-77) - Auto-save if threshold exceeded
- [manual_save(frame, detections, reason)](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/src/cheat_detection_web_app/app.py#293-315) - Manual save from UI
- [get_recent_events(limit)](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/src/detection/flagged_evidence_saver.py#322-336) - Retrieve event history
- [_cleanup_old_evidence()](file:///c:/Users/Mega_pc/Desktop/Exam-cheat-detection/src/detection/flagged_evidence_saver.py#283-321) - Enforce retention policy

